WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.067 --> 00:00:02.434
-It is so good to see you, bud.

00:00:02.434 --> 00:00:04.234
Congrats on the book.
-Thanks so much.

00:00:04.234 --> 00:00:06.434
-Number one. Not too shabby.
-Not bad, right?

00:00:06.434 --> 00:00:08.234
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:08.234 --> 00:00:10.534
-Can't get better than that.
-So happy. Very lucky.

00:00:10.534 --> 00:00:13.667
-Yeah, I wanted to talk to you,
because it's been such a --

00:00:13.667 --> 00:00:16.334
It's been an awful year.
-I know.

00:00:16.334 --> 00:00:17.767
Honestly, I just --

00:00:17.767 --> 00:00:21.033
So much has happened, and it's
been so rough for everybody.

00:00:21.033 --> 00:00:23.000
And you look back,
and you're like, "The pandemic?"

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:24.667
How long has it been?
I have no clue now.

00:00:24.667 --> 00:00:26.100
We say a year, but what is it?

00:00:26.100 --> 00:00:29.534
Like 18 months now. And I'm just
honestly happy to be here.

00:00:29.534 --> 00:00:31.267
I'm so -- I just feel so good.

00:00:31.267 --> 00:00:33.701
I'm ready for
this next year ahead.

00:00:33.701 --> 00:00:35.033
-Let's do it.
We're going to get there.

00:00:35.033 --> 00:00:36.501
-Yeah.

00:00:36.501 --> 00:00:38.934
-I saw an interview -- Or
I read an interview, actually.

00:00:38.934 --> 00:00:40.300
You were talking about this book

00:00:40.300 --> 00:00:42.067
and how this one
is very personal.

00:00:42.067 --> 00:00:44.200
-Yes. Oh, my goodness.
-You know I love the cookbooks.

00:00:44.200 --> 00:00:47.267
I love the other two. I love --
The photography is fantastic.

00:00:47.267 --> 00:00:49.801
-Thank you. Yes. Alex.
-Nails it.

00:00:49.801 --> 00:00:51.834
-Alex is an incredible
photographer.

00:00:51.834 --> 00:00:53.567
-This is the worst way
to hold the book. Sorry.

00:00:53.567 --> 00:00:55.434
"I love the photographer."

00:00:55.434 --> 00:00:58.167
-I wanted everything to be so
joyful and vibrant and bright.

00:00:58.167 --> 00:01:00.634
And I was like,
"This is -- It's a must."

00:01:00.634 --> 00:01:03.234
I want it to be colorful
and fun, I want the recipes

00:01:03.234 --> 00:01:05.868
to be comforting for people, and
it's everything that we needed

00:01:05.868 --> 00:01:07.400
in the time that we wrote it.

00:01:07.400 --> 00:01:09.467
-Food is always there for us.
-Yes, it is.

00:01:09.467 --> 00:01:12.033
-No matter what we go through.
-It's the one constant.

00:01:12.033 --> 00:01:13.801
-It really is.
It's the one thing.

00:01:13.801 --> 00:01:15.000
And you go -- You know,

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:16.501
and if it's comfort food,
it's comfort food.

00:01:16.501 --> 00:01:18.767
If it's mac and cheese,
it's mac and cheese.

00:01:18.767 --> 00:01:20.901
-This is all, like, food
to eat on the couch, basically.

00:01:20.901 --> 00:01:23.267
-Yes! That's what we want!

00:01:23.267 --> 00:01:25.167
[ Cheers and applause ]
-That's all I want.

00:01:25.167 --> 00:01:26.834
-Is there one ingredient
that we'll never see

00:01:26.834 --> 00:01:28.300
in a Chrissy Teigen cookbook?

00:01:28.300 --> 00:01:30.834
-Well, this is the issue.

00:01:30.834 --> 00:01:32.734
Because I obviously
have to create for everybody.

00:01:32.734 --> 00:01:34.767
So I'm like, "Ugh.
Other people like things."

00:01:34.767 --> 00:01:37.167
I have to put it in there,
but I genuinely think, like,

00:01:37.167 --> 00:01:39.968
if the devil had a garden,
he would grow beets.

00:01:39.968 --> 00:01:43.033
[ Scattered applause ]

00:01:43.033 --> 00:01:44.901
-No! It's a divided audience.
Really?

00:01:44.901 --> 00:01:47.934
-It was a divided audience.
Like, golden beets are good.

00:01:47.934 --> 00:01:49.767
So I have a recipe
where I use golden ones.

00:01:49.767 --> 00:01:51.601
But they need to be really
sugared up and everything.

00:01:51.601 --> 00:01:53.601
The red ones
are just, like, vile.

00:01:53.601 --> 00:01:55.400
Vile! I don't know.
They taste like dirt.

00:01:55.400 --> 00:01:57.100
-I don't think my wife
likes beets, either.

00:01:57.100 --> 00:01:59.467
-Yeah, they're bad.
-I like beets.

00:01:59.467 --> 00:02:01.634
-I don't think they're supposed
to be eaten, honestly.

00:02:01.634 --> 00:02:03.534
Really?
-Yeah! Like, pickled beets.

00:02:03.534 --> 00:02:05.400
-I heard you don't like
mayonnaise, either.

00:02:05.400 --> 00:02:11.434
So that is -- And I think mayo
is the binder of all things.

00:02:11.434 --> 00:02:14.267
-Mayonnaise is --
Even the name is --

00:02:14.267 --> 00:02:16.033
-Oh, I go to Subway,
I'm like, "Extra mayo."

00:02:16.033 --> 00:02:19.167
Extra "mayonnaise."
-Oh, no, they changed the name.

00:02:19.167 --> 00:02:21.167
They try to make it young
like, "Hey, we're mayo."

00:02:21.167 --> 00:02:23.601
You're like, "Hey."
Just call yourself Meta.

00:02:23.601 --> 00:02:25.467
It's fine. We get it.
-It's so good!

00:02:25.467 --> 00:02:27.501
[ Laughter ]

00:02:27.501 --> 00:02:30.100
Metanaise.
-Metanaise. You'll see.

00:02:30.100 --> 00:02:31.300
It's going to come out like,

00:02:31.300 --> 00:02:32.534
"Oh, we're aioli.
We're traveled."

00:02:32.534 --> 00:02:33.968
Like, oh, please.
-I know!

00:02:33.968 --> 00:02:36.400
I won't do "french fries
in the mayo" thing.

00:02:36.400 --> 00:02:39.767
But mayo -- I feel like
it binds the flavors of things.

00:02:39.767 --> 00:02:42.367
I'm gonna get you to like it.
-I know. I can grow out of it.

00:02:42.367 --> 00:02:45.267
I went to a wedding once,
and I was just so hungry,

00:02:45.267 --> 00:02:47.300
and it was one of
the longest services ever.

00:02:47.300 --> 00:02:48.934
And I'm --
You know, I grew up Catholic.

00:02:48.934 --> 00:02:50.834
There were, like,
extra steps in this wedding.

00:02:50.834 --> 00:02:52.501
I was,
"I never heard of this step."

00:02:52.501 --> 00:02:54.767
I'm like -- I was so hungry.
And we got to the reception.

00:02:54.767 --> 00:02:56.834
We had to get in a bus
to go to the reception,

00:02:56.834 --> 00:02:58.601
up a hill and all this stuff.

00:02:58.601 --> 00:03:00.234
I go, "I already
put in the work, man."

00:03:00.234 --> 00:03:02.100
And I get there, and they go,
"French fries."

00:03:02.100 --> 00:03:03.667
I go, "Oh, my God, yes!"

00:03:03.667 --> 00:03:06.033
And they came in a cone
with mayonnaise on the bottom.

00:03:06.033 --> 00:03:07.200
-No!

00:03:07.200 --> 00:03:09.267
-Pre-dipped and soaked
in mayonnaise?

00:03:09.267 --> 00:03:11.367
Well, don't you hate
when you go to a wedding --

00:03:11.367 --> 00:03:13.701
-We're never invited
to weddings.

00:03:13.701 --> 00:03:16.968
I think people assume
that we can't go,

00:03:16.968 --> 00:03:19.200
so we really don't get
very many invites.

00:03:19.200 --> 00:03:21.667
-Really?
I don't want to go anymore.

00:03:21.667 --> 00:03:24.133
-No, I love --
I like them a lot.

00:03:24.133 --> 00:03:25.868
-You do?
-Yeah, I do.

00:03:25.868 --> 00:03:27.334
But then there's always like,

00:03:27.334 --> 00:03:29.901
"Oh, my, there just
happens to be a piano."

00:03:29.901 --> 00:03:31.300
And then you're like...

00:03:31.300 --> 00:03:32.934
-"Ah, John, yeah.
You know, can you...?"

00:03:32.934 --> 00:03:35.267
-Yes. Every time. Yeah.
"That's so crazy."

00:03:35.267 --> 00:03:37.334
-"That's so weird
that there's a piano here

00:03:37.334 --> 00:03:40.434
on the back of this bus.
Why would a piano...?

00:03:40.434 --> 00:03:42.901
John, do you want
to play maybe one?"

00:03:42.901 --> 00:03:45.300
[ Laughter ]
Halloween's this weekend.

00:03:45.300 --> 00:03:47.801
Since you're a mom
and a cookbook author,

00:03:47.801 --> 00:03:49.834
your opinion on this
is very, very important

00:03:49.834 --> 00:03:51.067
to the world right now.

00:03:51.067 --> 00:03:53.167
How do you feel
about candy corn?

00:03:53.167 --> 00:03:56.701
-Oh, no. Okay, I -- Okay.

00:03:56.701 --> 00:03:59.167
-Here we go. Tell me.
-I saw a tweet.

00:03:59.167 --> 00:04:02.968
You know, people on Twitter
love to be mad at candy corn,

00:04:02.968 --> 00:04:05.534
and I had typed out a tweet
where I said,

00:04:05.534 --> 00:04:08.434
"I don't know, guys.
I kind of like it."

00:04:08.434 --> 00:04:12.701
And when I say "kind of,"
I really like candy corn.

00:04:12.701 --> 00:04:14.501
-You really like candy corn?

00:04:14.501 --> 00:04:17.133
-I had typed this out, and then
I was like, "I can't say this.

00:04:17.133 --> 00:04:18.801
It's too controversial."

00:04:18.801 --> 00:04:21.234
Like, it really is.
Of all the things I've done.

00:04:21.234 --> 00:04:23.067
And I'm like, "No!"

00:04:23.067 --> 00:04:24.567
-You didn't send it out?

00:04:24.567 --> 00:04:26.133
The audience
seems to be with you.

00:04:26.133 --> 00:04:27.434
-Do you guys like candy corn?

00:04:27.434 --> 00:04:29.501
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:29.501 --> 00:04:32.767
I think it tastes like
a buttery Mrs. Butterworth.

00:04:32.767 --> 00:04:35.133
Like, to me, it tastes
like a delicious syrup,

00:04:35.133 --> 00:04:36.801
and I bite the white tip off
and --

00:04:36.801 --> 00:04:38.334
Do you think there's
different flavors? No.

00:04:38.334 --> 00:04:40.601
-I try to imagine that there
are, but, no, they're not.

00:04:40.601 --> 00:04:42.167
No, right? No, they're all --

00:04:42.167 --> 00:04:44.100
All three colors are
just three -- the same.

00:04:44.100 --> 00:04:45.400
-White, yellow, and orange.

00:04:45.400 --> 00:04:47.667
-It's just candle wax,
candle wax, candle wax.

00:04:47.667 --> 00:04:48.868
-No!
-Yes!

00:04:48.868 --> 00:04:50.567
-No, it's good.
And the pumpkin-shaped ones?

00:04:50.567 --> 00:04:52.868
Do you like those ones?
They're so good!

00:04:52.868 --> 00:04:54.934
-I feel like the pumpkin-shaped
ones are candy corns

00:04:54.934 --> 00:04:57.801
that went to
Witness Protection Program.

00:04:57.801 --> 00:04:59.968
"We're not candy corns.
We're pumpkins."

00:04:59.968 --> 00:05:02.033
-"We'll change the shape."
-Yeah, exactly.

00:05:02.033 --> 00:05:04.000
Here's what I like
about the book.

00:05:04.000 --> 00:05:06.067
Because not only
is it great recipes

00:05:06.067 --> 00:05:07.601
and I know it comes from love

00:05:07.601 --> 00:05:09.133
and I know
you actually make these,

00:05:09.133 --> 00:05:12.701
but there's also a bonus recipe
at the end after, like,

00:05:12.701 --> 00:05:14.634
all the credits --
like a Marvel movie.

00:05:14.634 --> 00:05:16.634
You finish the movie,
and then it's like,

00:05:16.634 --> 00:05:18.133
"Oh, here's your Easter egg."

00:05:18.133 --> 00:05:20.634
And then there's another
little bonus recipe there.

00:05:20.634 --> 00:05:22.501
Now, what is this one?

00:05:22.501 --> 00:05:24.934
-This is essentially --
Well, I love even numbers.

00:05:24.934 --> 00:05:26.868
I had an odd number of recipes
in the book.

00:05:26.868 --> 00:05:28.334
And then I figured marijuana

00:05:28.334 --> 00:05:30.367
has been legalized
in so many states,

00:05:30.367 --> 00:05:32.501
so why not just give something
for the high people?

00:05:32.501 --> 00:05:33.801
-Okay. All right.

00:05:33.801 --> 00:05:35.234
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:35.234 --> 00:05:37.667
All right.
Can you explain what it is?

00:05:37.667 --> 00:05:40.434
-This is essentially Gardetto's

00:05:40.434 --> 00:05:43.334
tossed in butter
stuffed into a pita.

00:05:43.334 --> 00:05:45.534
-So it's basically like
Chex Mix in a pita?

00:05:45.534 --> 00:05:47.400
-Yeah, it's some
buttered Gardetto's.

00:05:47.400 --> 00:05:49.634
-All right.
So you put some butter in there?

00:05:49.634 --> 00:05:50.801
-Yeah.

00:05:50.801 --> 00:05:52.701
-All right.
Let's try this together.

00:05:52.701 --> 00:05:54.434
Good luck, buddy.
Happy Halloween.

00:05:54.434 --> 00:05:56.934
-This is not what the book is --
The book is real recipes.

00:05:56.934 --> 00:05:58.200
-Oh, no. Legit.

00:05:58.200 --> 00:05:59.901
But I just thought
it would be funny to eat this.

00:05:59.901 --> 00:06:01.334
-Cheers.
-Congratulations on number one.

00:06:01.334 --> 00:06:04.534
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Not bad. Not bad.

00:06:06.501 --> 00:06:10.467
A little dry.
-Not bad. I like it.

00:06:10.467 --> 00:06:14.801
-"Cravings: All together"
is available now.

00:06:14.801 --> 00:06:18.467
When we come back...
Chrissy and I...

00:06:18.467 --> 00:06:21.801
are going head-to-head
in a game of "Pup Quiz."

